{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/711705-deva-s-public-face","id":711705,"title":"Deva's public face","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-20T20:37:14-07:00","id":711705,"title":"Deva's public face","content":"I want to include Deva in my game, but I'm not sure how they appear to the outside world. I would think that they have human employees that are completely unaware of their god machine related tasks. I'm not sure the books published thus far describe this. I am even considering allowing players to become employees of Deva (without telling them anything about it). Any suggestions or headcannon on what they do publicly? and how I can make them seem like a real company?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T20:45:55-07:00","id":711730,"title":"","content":"My impression from the Seattle section of the core book is that they come off very much like a big tech company of the Apple/Google type to outsiders. If you've ever read The Circle by Dave Eggers, basically that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T02:14:27-07:00","id":712096,"title":"","content":"They seem to have a lower profile and perhaps more of a nuanced public image than, say, Cheiron, but entirely able to go toe to toe with them in terms of resources and money.<br /> <br /> They come across as a big multinational; fingers in lots of different lies. For a modern comparison I'd maybe suggest E/Evil Corp from Mr Robot. Just with a slightly tighter purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T06:33:24-07:00","id":712328,"title":"","content":"What does Deva do publically? <a href=\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/tenbu-technologies#/entity\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.crunchbase.com/organizat...logies#/entity</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Tenbu&quot; is roughly the japanese equivalent to the word &quot;deva.&quot; So, in my games, I actually consider them to be a company owned by Deva Corporation umbrella company. I also have made up companies that specialize in medicine and construction for Deva, and use those. <br /> <br /> Remember, all of the God Machine's projects piggy back on existing human structures. Everything looks normal, just with the occasional odd prjoect mixed in with a bunch of others. Deva Corp does all the same thing regular companies do, with just a bit more research on the Gears on the side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T11:18:47-07:00","id":712767,"title":"","content":"They have oodles of cash, so that can afford PR, publicity, marketing and lobbying. They have access to Embeds and Exploits (Courtesy of some poor bastard Unchained, or a recruited Fractal or Offspring) like You Can Tell Me, Sermon and Urban Legend. They can control how the outside world sees them, to a frightening extent.<br /> <br /> Above all else, they're a <i>cult</i>, just as much (perhaps even more) as a business. While they have smiling recruiters at all the best colleges, looking for the best and the brightest, offering high salaries, excellent benefits, challenging workplace, etc. there are levels of initiation within the company. As employees are promoted, they're also screened to see if they would be receptive to learning the truth of the G-M... in small doses at a time.<br /> <br /> Look at some of the full page adds that Lockheed-Martin puts in magazines like the Economist. For that matter, I'm sure that Deva Corp has any number of lucrative defense contracts...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:27:03-07:00","id":743196,"title":"","content":"Don't forget supernatural merits, the G-M can give out supernatural merits after all, so they undoubtedly have telepaths, telekinetics, and the like on the payroll.<br /> <br /> When one can read minds and arrange for &quot;accidents&quot; I imagine makes getting your way rather easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 10-30-2015, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:47:11-07:00","id":743325,"title":"","content":"&quot;So, your people were gifted with the power to read minds and alter fate by an incomprehensible machine-god... and your division uses them to rig insurance rates. I got that right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}